submission/devpost-story.md:21:- **Any source:** selected text (right-click), the whole page (readability extraction), a PDF open in the tab, a YouTube video's transcript, a screenshot or image, or pasted notes.
submission/devpost-story.md:24:- **Privacy mode:** one toggle switches the router to `ONLY_ON_DEVICE`; nothing leaves the machine.
submission/devpost-story.md:25:- **Offline queue:** jobs that genuinely need the cloud while you're offline are queued and run automatically when you reconnect; on-device jobs keep working offline.
submission/devpost-story.md:29:- **Source anchors:** each card links back to the exact passage via a text-fragment URL.
submission/devpost-story.md:42:- **Choosing the mode per request, not per app.** `PREFER_ON_DEVICE` alone hides important decisions (a PDF silently goes to the cloud). We built the router on top so users can see and control those decisions.
submission/devpost-story.md:43:- **The on-device token budget.** Long pages exceed the 9,216-token on-device limit; we chunk with overlap, de-duplicate across chunks, and fall back to a long-context cloud model when content isn't sensitive.
