 | --- | --- |
 | Privacy mode or Only on-device | Require Gemini Nano. Split long text into local chunks. Show an error for unavailable Nano or unsupported media. |
 | Sensitive text | Keep it on-device. If only the pattern check fired and Nano is unavailable, ask before sending this capture to cloud. Privacy mode and Only on-device keep the capture local. |
-| Short text or supported image with Nano ready in Auto | Run on-device directly. The default input budget is 6,000 estimated tokens, with 1,500 reserved for output. CJK text is estimated at roughly one token per character. |
-| Long text | Use the long-document cloud model when online in Auto. Split into local chunks if Nano is ready and the capture is offline, private, or set to Prefer on-device. |
+| Short, nonsensitive text or PNG/JPEG in Auto | Prefer Gemini Nano through Firebase AI Logic. Firebase can fall back to cloud when Nano is unavailable. The default input budget is 6,000 estimated tokens, with 1,500 reserved for output. CJK text is estimated at roughly one token per character. |
+| Long text | Prefer the long-document cloud model when online in Auto. Split into local chunks if Nano is ready and the capture is offline, private, or set to Prefer on-device. Chunks overlap by about 10% at sentence boundaries where possible. Margin deduplicates cards across chunks. |
 | Scanned PDF or video without accessible captions | Use the long-document cloud model. Margin extracts readable PDF text or captions locally when available. |
 | Nano unavailable for a cloud-eligible capture | Use the cloud when online. Downloadable and downloading states point to **Enable on-device AI**. |
-| Cloud needed while offline | Queue the capture locally. The open side panel reroutes it on reconnect and retries failures with 30-second and 60-second delays. After three failed attempts, the entry shows **Failed** with a manual retry in Options. |
+| Cloud needed while offline | Queue the capture locally. Keep the side panel open for automatic retries when you're online. It reroutes on reconnect and retries failures with 30-second and 60-second delays. After three failed attempts, the entry shows **Failed** with a manual retry in Options. |
 | Typed answer during review | Check with Nano only. Manual reveal and self-rating are always available. |
 
 The sensitivity gate combines patterns with local text classification on eligible cloud routes when Nano is available. A malformed classification is treated as sensitive. In the side panel, expand **AI routing explained** to see the active input budget, models, sensitivity setting, and cards per chunk.
@@ -106,7 +109,7 @@
 
 ## Privacy
 
-Cards, route history, queued source material, and review history live in this Chrome profile. On-device generation and typed-answer grading keep their input on the device. Cloud routes send the selected source content or media to Firebase AI Logic and the Gemini API. Privacy mode keeps inference local, and a configured build may still retrieve Firebase Remote Config settings. Margin uses temporary Chrome tab access for captures and requests access to a particular site when a page or PDF needs additional permission. You can manage granted site access in Chrome’s extension settings.
+Cards, route history, queued source material, and review history live in this Chrome profile. On-device generation and typed-answer grading keep their input on the device. Cloud routes send the selected source content or media to Firebase AI Logic and the Gemini API. In Privacy mode, no source content leaves your machine. When Firebase is configured and Demo mode is off, Margin still fetches routing settings from Firebase Remote Config. Margin uses temporary Chrome tab access for captures and requests access to a particular site when a page or PDF needs additional permission. You can manage granted site access in Chrome’s extension settings.
 
